
"Rune1a" "As you stare at this rune, an image forms in your mind. You see a weary man trudging through these caverns, intent on finding the secret portal."
"Rune1b" "As you stare at this rune, an image forms in your mind. You see a weary man trudging through these caverns, intent on finding the secret portal."
"Rune2a" "As you stare at this rune, an image forms in your mind. You see a man betrayed, pushed into a flow of lava by the man he had thought was his best friend."
"Rune2b" "As you stare at this rune, an image forms in your mind. You see a man betrayed, pushed into a flow of lava by the man he had thought was his best friend."
"Rune3a" "As you stare at this rune, an image forms in your mind. You see a burnt human figure pulled out of a lava flow by the strange Magmites that haunt these caverns."
"Rune3b" "As you stare at this rune, an image forms in your mind. You see a burnt human figure pulled out of a lava flow by the strange Magmites that haunt these caverns."
"Rune4a" "As you stare at this rune, an image forms in your mind. You see a figure most terrible. Half human, half lava, this can only be the Magmites' master."
"Rune4b" "As you stare at this rune, an image forms in your mind. You see a figure most terrible. Half human, half lava, this can only be the Magmites' master."
"Rune4c" "As you stare at this rune, an image forms in your mind. You see a figure most terrible. Half human, half lava, this can only be the Magmites' master."
"Page1" "September 12, 1921<br><br>Janssen claims he has found a great cavern under an American city. Can it be, truly, the Cavern of Transcendence? I hardly dare hope, and yet I must journey there and see it for myself.<br><br>Ingelbert Maahs"
"Page2" "September 22, 1921<br><br>I have arrived in Paragon City. I can hardly wait to set eyes on the cavern, to see if it is truly contains the portal I have sought for so very long. Janssen shares my enthusiams. He suggested we get started right away.<br><br>Ingelbert Maahs	"
"Page3" "September 24, 1921<br><br>We have been journeying in these caverns for more than two days now. I am beginning to give up hope that we will ever set eyes upon the portal. But Janssen insists his calculations are correct. In truth, he has grown distant. I am beginning to wonder if my old friend has changed.<br><br>Ingelbert Maahs"
"Page4" "September 25, 1921<br><br>Janssen will not talk. Perhaps he is delirious? When I pointed out that we had only enough provisions for one of us to make the return journey, he shrugged and would not answer.<br><br>I am afraid.<br><br>Ingelbert Maahs"
